# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Zachary A. H. Goodwin et al. (2024). Transferability and Accuracy of Ionic Liquid Simulations with Equivariant Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials.
#   The Journal of Physical Chemistry Letters. doi:10.1021/acs.jpclett.4c01942  arXiv:2403.01980v3
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2403.01980v3 (sha256 cfe4fc14a9047e00...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 141 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: (i) the Allegro model for the ionic liquid
# [F-OMIM][C4F9CO2] with its settings and reference DFT, and (ii) the
# compositional-transferability test on the solid electrolyte LPSCl
# (seven models trained on all combinations of three compositions, each
# tested on all three; SI Tables S9 and S10). The salt-in-ionic-liquid
# transferability tests are figures and further SI tables, see gaps.
# Read from the arXiv preprint (v3).

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

