###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The LPSCl tables sit in the SI section 'Compositional Transferability with Allegro'; the architecture and hyperparameters of these seven models are not restated there, so the runs apply Allegro without settings. Test sets are 6, 4 and 5 frames (tiny); training sizes are the stated 52, 33 and 47 frames per composition, summed for combinations. Pseudopotential type of the VASP calculations is not stated.
# - Not encoded: the NequIP transferability test on classical (OPLS) data of Li[PF6] in [EMIM][PF6] (Fig. 1; rmax = 5, lmax = 1, 5 layers, learning rate 0.05, batch 5), the Allegro tests on classical and DFT data (Tables S2 to S7; rmax = 6, lmax = 2, 2 layers, learning rate 0.0005, batch 1), the hyperparameter scan of Table S12, the stress-scale and volume-scan tables (S13, S14), and the densities, thermal expansion and compressibility against experiment.
# - No accuracy figures are encoded for the ionic-liquid production model; its per-element force MAEs are in SI tables keyed by a hyperparameter code and were not matched to the final model with certainty.
# - Read from the arXiv v3 preprint; arXiv id matched by title and author.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

